[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2422285560","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98284#issuecomment-2422285560","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98284","id":2422285560,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QYST4","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-18T11:48:13Z","updated_at":"2024-10-18T11:49:00Z","body":"Worth pointing out that under the original design proposed by @reduz in #90400, the introduction of thread guards is very much intentional to catch any race condition errors (before there was simply a global mutex hiding unintentional behavior), so we're basically seeing that system in action here.\r\n\r\nI've not reviewed in detail how the multi-threaded render driver works but the thread creating the device will be the one assigned exclusive access to the functions mentioned in the error, so it's gonna be important to verify if this is being respected or not.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2422285560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2422426284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98284#issuecomment-2422426284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98284","id":2422426284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QY0qs","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-18T13:01:04Z","updated_at":"2024-10-18T13:01:04Z","body":"It seems the issue is pretty straightforward.\r\n\r\nOne thread creates the RenderingDevice and the other uses it. Each Display Server handles the creation and initialization of Rendering Device. The thread Id is stored locally on the constructor. This thread is different than the dedicated render thread used for it.\r\n\r\nI'll tag @RandomShaper and see if he's got any ideas on how to handle this correctly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.g